{"id":470,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"Cells similar to those of plants have been found in its fur. Its hard tail can fell a large tree with one stroke, and the tail's sharpness exceeds even that of a sword crafted by a master."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"This Pokémon’s tail is blade sharp, with a fantastic cutting edge that can slice right though large trees."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Galarians favor the distinctive aroma that drifts from this Pokémon’s leaves. There’s a popular perfume made using that scent."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It gets its nutrition from photosynthesis. It lives a quiet life deep in forests where clean rivers flow."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Although it doesn’t like disputes, it will sharpen the leaf on its tail into a blade and fight if it has to protect its friends."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"The younger they are, the more they smell like fresh grass. With age, their fragrance takes on the odor of fallen leaves."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Its cellular composition is closer to that of a plant than an animal. It uses photosynthesis to produce its energy supply without eating food."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Just like a plant, it uses photosynthesis. As a result, it is always enveloped in clear air."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"When you see Leafeon asleep in a patch of sunshine, you’ll know it is using photosynthesis to produce clean air."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"With cells similar to those of plants, it performs photosynthesis inside its body and creates pure air."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"It basically does not fight. With cells similar to those of plants, it can perform photosynthesis."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Leaf Guard","hidden":false,"description":"Prevents status conditions in harsh sunlight."},{"name":"Chlorophyll","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in harsh sunlight."}